1
00:00:58,637 --> 00:01:02,283
4x06 The WeHo Ho

2
00:01:08,607 --> 00:01:11,012
Subtitles: swsub.com

3
00:01:13,362 --> 00:01:15,931
Hello, E, what a pleasant
pick-me-up start to my morning.

4
00:01:16,218 --> 00:01:17,675
Yeah, blow me too, Ari.

5
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:18,815
Whoo, sugar mouth!

6
00:01:18,910 --> 00:01:20,742
All the blood just rushed
to my power source.

7
00:01:20,761 --> 00:01:21,777
What's up?

8
00:01:21,834 --> 00:01:23,483
We don't want to do
the movie with Walsh.

9
00:01:23,559 --> 00:01:24,745
- What do you mean?
- I said,

10
00:01:24,785 --> 00:01:27,019
- We want to find another director.
- Another director?

11
00:01:27,098 --> 00:01:30,172
Are you out of your mind?
What, has Walsh been teasing you again?

12
00:01:30,257 --> 00:01:31,846
The guy called me a liar and a thief.

13
00:01:32,398 --> 00:01:33,636
Sticks and stones.

14
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:36,395
You can't throw away a movie
just 'cause you can't get along.

15
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:39,276
It's Vince's decision,
not mine, Ari, so let's move on.

16
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:42,204
I don't think you realize
that I pulled off a miracle here.

17
00:01:42,322 --> 00:01:45,160
<i>48 hours ago,
Vince was unemployable.</i>

18
00:01:45,301 --> 00:01:47,939
He wants to do the movie,
but not with Walsh. What's the big deal?

19
00:01:47,991 --> 00:01:50,500
The big deal is
I sold them on a package...

20
00:01:50,681 --> 00:01:52,215
The <i>Medellin</i> package.

21
00:01:52,344 --> 00:01:54,451
We start saying that part
of that package is no good

22
00:01:54,525 --> 00:01:57,318
and they start asking questions
that we're not prepared to answer,

23
00:01:57,447 --> 00:01:59,723
like "is <i>Medellin</i> really that good?"

24
00:01:59,952 --> 00:02:02,197
<i>do you want to answer that, E?</i>

25
00:02:02,855 --> 00:02:04,443
That's what I thought. Now...

26
00:02:04,598 --> 00:02:07,106
You're supposed to be
in Dana Gordon's office this afternoon.

27
00:02:07,231 --> 00:02:10,179
<i>I want you to talk to
Vince again before I cancel.</i>

28
00:02:10,272 --> 00:02:12,341
I parted the Red Sea for you, E.

29
00:02:12,508 --> 00:02:14,034
Don't piss on the sand.

30
00:02:15,287 --> 00:02:17,280
- That Ari?
- Yep. He's not happy.

31
00:02:17,823 --> 00:02:19,594
You are gonna be delighted
when you taste

32
00:02:19,698 --> 00:02:22,033
these fresh,
hand-picked strawberry waffles.

33
00:02:22,368 --> 00:02:24,954
- Nice. Where do you pick waffles from?
- Clever, E.

34
00:02:25,264 --> 00:02:27,566
Look at that big fat bad boy
I saved just for you.

35
00:02:27,702 --> 00:02:29,099
Thank you very much, Drama.

36
00:02:31,455 --> 00:02:33,291
- Walsh again.
- You gonna answer?

37
00:02:33,484 --> 00:02:36,641
Well, let's see. His last email :
"Admit you leaked my trailer and die."

38
00:02:36,745 --> 00:02:39,325
- So no, I don't think so.
- Fuck Ari if he's not happy.

39
00:02:39,862 --> 00:02:41,444
We obviously can't work like this.

40
00:02:41,522 --> 00:02:43,290
Which is too bad
because <i>Lost in the Clouds</i>

41
00:02:43,362 --> 00:02:45,430
would have been a great
movie with Billy directing.

42
00:02:45,456 --> 00:02:48,249
We'll find another great director,
even if I have to find him myself.

43
00:02:48,304 --> 00:02:51,252
Anyone interested in driving out
to Palmdale to see my cousin Ronnie?

44
00:02:52,182 --> 00:02:54,018
Haven't we been through
this already, Turtle?

45
00:02:54,096 --> 00:02:56,908
I'm telling you, guys, he says
he has a little money-making venture.

46
00:02:56,976 --> 00:02:58,804
And in my house,
when cousin Ronnie talks,

47
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:00,924
like E.F. Hutton,
you better fuckin' listen.

48
00:03:01,044 --> 00:03:02,967
Why do you have so much
confidence in him again?

49
00:03:03,019 --> 00:03:05,812
Are you kidding? You know the guy
always knew how to make a buck.

50
00:03:05,952 --> 00:03:09,036
You don't remember? He was the first
guy on our block to have a foreign car.

51
00:03:09,076 --> 00:03:10,722
The first guy to have an in-ground pool.

52
00:03:10,864 --> 00:03:12,490
The first guy to have aluminum siding.

53
00:03:12,558 --> 00:03:15,183
Yeah, and the first guy to have
it all seized by the government.

54
00:03:15,390 --> 00:03:16,890
That's 'cause he didn't pay his taxes

55
00:03:16,942 --> 00:03:18,675
not 'cause
he wasn't rollin' in the green.

56
00:03:18,778 --> 00:03:20,240
What's the investment opportunity?

57
00:03:20,318 --> 00:03:22,412
Now he wouldn't say
on the phone, which means...

58
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,402
He's on the inside, as usual.

59
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:26,449
- Now, who's in?
- Not me.

60
00:03:26,828 --> 00:03:28,768
I'll drive out
to the desert with you, Turtle,

61
00:03:28,923 --> 00:03:30,656
maybe hit the outlets along the way.

62
00:03:31,006 --> 00:03:32,997
But don't count on me
parting with any cash.

63
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:34,824
Like I ever do.

64
00:03:45,886 --> 00:03:48,498
- Is there a fax waiting for me?
- I don't think so.

65
00:03:48,537 --> 00:03:51,329
Just got off the phone with Dana.
She said she sent over Vinny's offer

66
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:52,845
- an hour ago.
- I haven't seen it.

67
00:03:53,027 --> 00:03:55,561
Well, get up, open your eyes wide
and go find it.

68
00:03:55,639 --> 00:03:56,906
Zoom zoom.

69
00:04:02,771 --> 00:04:03,961
Hey, dumbfuck!

70
00:04:06,033 --> 00:04:07,636
Please don't be mean to me today.

71
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,714
Is this not an offer
with Vinny's name on it?

72
00:04:10,435 --> 00:04:12,064
Yes, it is. I apologize.

73
00:04:12,245 --> 00:04:13,409
What's wrong with you?

74
00:04:14,887 --> 00:04:15,947
Speak!

75
00:04:16,095 --> 00:04:18,060
- Tom broke up with me.
- Oh, Jesus.

76
00:04:18,259 --> 00:04:19,448
And I don't know what to do.

77
00:04:19,487 --> 00:04:20,886
Well, I tell you what you don't do:

78
00:04:20,937 --> 00:04:23,523
you don't bring it into work
and you don't bring it to me, okay?

79
00:04:23,601 --> 00:04:26,022
Because you know that me thinking
about you and tom doing...

80
00:04:26,126 --> 00:04:27,203
You know, makes me sick.

81
00:04:27,311 --> 00:04:31,169
So let's focus on work and not on Tom
and everything's going to be okay. Okay?

82
00:04:32,171 --> 00:04:33,386
Get E on the horn

83
00:04:33,546 --> 00:04:35,795
so I can tell him
Vinny is the six million dollar man.

84
00:04:35,911 --> 00:04:38,053
That should knock some sense into him.
Maybe.

85
00:04:38,988 --> 00:04:40,540
How long should I just sit in here?

86
00:04:40,643 --> 00:04:42,764
Oh, I forgot to tell you...
your 10:00 a.m. Is here.

87
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:44,626
Your forgot to tell me
I had a 10:00 a.m.

88
00:04:48,487 --> 00:04:50,085
How are you, mr. Walsh?

89
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:53,581
I'll tell you after you tell me
what kind of deal I'm gonna get

90
00:04:53,786 --> 00:04:55,234
if I let you be my agent.

91
00:04:56,840 --> 00:04:58,081
When I spoke to you yesterday,

92
00:04:58,107 --> 00:05:00,642
you didn't tell me that there
was a problem between you and E.

93
00:05:00,693 --> 00:05:03,478
Now, unless you handle that,
there's not gonna be any deal

94
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:05,303
and I'm not gonna
be able to represent you.

95
00:05:05,364 --> 00:05:07,071
I've been trying
to handle it all morning,

96
00:05:07,161 --> 00:05:09,670
but I can't get the pale prick
on the phone. Maybe you can.

97
00:05:10,601 --> 00:05:13,264
I'm sure I can.
That's what I do. I connect people.

98
00:05:18,671 --> 00:05:19,809
Give me one second.

99
00:05:21,664 --> 00:05:23,293
Lloyd! Snap out of it.

100
00:05:23,423 --> 00:05:24,457
Did you call E?

101
00:05:25,078 --> 00:05:26,159
Call now. Forget the offer.

102
00:05:26,211 --> 00:05:28,538
Ask him if he and Vince will
please come here immediately.

103
00:05:28,590 --> 00:05:30,374
And tell him
that I used the word "please".

104
00:05:31,124 --> 00:05:32,236
- But Ari?
- Yes?

105
00:05:32,507 --> 00:05:33,671
Do you mind dialing?

106
00:05:33,749 --> 00:05:36,723
In my traumatized state this morning,
I forgot to put in my contacts.

107
00:05:37,877 --> 00:05:39,015
Billy, I'll be right there.

108
00:05:39,092 --> 00:05:41,688
Why do you have to be so skeptical
about everything?

109
00:05:41,921 --> 00:05:43,578
Only because I care about you,

110
00:05:43,681 --> 00:05:45,802
and I don't want to see
your little hopes get dashed.

111
00:05:45,869 --> 00:05:47,846
You're just jealous
'cause you never cashed in

112
00:05:47,913 --> 00:05:50,019
on any of cousin Ronnie's
windfalls in the past.

113
00:05:50,148 --> 00:05:51,933
My talent is my windfall.

114
00:05:52,006 --> 00:05:55,946
And you, sadly, and I mean no disrespect
by this, don't have a talent.

115
00:05:56,075 --> 00:05:58,066
So, for you to take
all your cash and to flush...

116
00:05:58,144 --> 00:05:59,916
My talent is knowing my limitations,

117
00:05:59,994 --> 00:06:02,037
which is why
I'm only putting half my money in.

118
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:03,537
So don't sweat it.

119
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:05,513
This is the place.

120
00:06:05,887 --> 00:06:07,568
- This is where he's staying?
- Yep.

121
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,660
Oh, yeah. He's rolling in it.

122
00:06:10,821 --> 00:06:12,089
Get out of the car, you punk!

123
00:06:13,938 --> 00:06:16,447
- You scared the hell out of me...
- What's up?

124
00:06:16,749 --> 00:06:18,120
What, now that you're a big celeb,

125
00:06:18,172 --> 00:06:20,370
I'm sure this shit happens
to you all the time, right?

126
00:06:20,732 --> 00:06:22,025
Congrats on the show.

127
00:06:22,206 --> 00:06:24,114
- You been watching?
- I have. It's terrible.

128
00:06:24,331 --> 00:06:26,089
Eh, but I heard
the networks pay big bucks,

129
00:06:26,141 --> 00:06:27,564
so who gives a fuck, right?

130
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,946
- Turtle, come here. Give me a hug!
- How are you?

131
00:06:29,998 --> 00:06:31,239
- Good.
- What's going on?

132
00:06:31,317 --> 00:06:32,842
Ah, you know, just wheelin' and deal'.

133
00:06:32,920 --> 00:06:34,342
So, what do you got for us?

134
00:06:35,061 --> 00:06:37,097
Let's go upstairs.
I don't want to talk out here.

135
00:06:37,806 --> 00:06:39,306
Good to see you guys, man!

136
00:06:39,799 --> 00:06:41,651
- Great to see you.
- This your car, Ronnie?

137
00:06:42,435 --> 00:06:43,525
Dick.

138
00:06:43,706 --> 00:06:46,163
I'm just saying,
don't let Ari get to you.

139
00:06:46,275 --> 00:06:48,506
- Why would he get to me?
- iI he yells at you, I mean.

140
00:06:48,574 --> 00:06:50,308
All of the sudden I'm Mr. Sensitive?

141
00:06:50,941 --> 00:06:53,010
You have been getting
in a lot of fights lately.

142
00:06:53,133 --> 00:06:54,426
I won't let him get to me.

143
00:06:54,683 --> 00:06:56,261
- You promise?
- I promise.

144
00:06:56,867 --> 00:06:58,005
Motherfucker!

145
00:06:59,231 --> 00:07:01,016
- What the fuck is this?
- I have no idea.

146
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,705
Just take it easy.
He comes bringing peace.

147
00:07:03,744 --> 00:07:05,554
- I'm waving the white flag, suit.
- Why?

148
00:07:05,654 --> 00:07:07,258
Because I was wrong and I'm sorry.

149
00:07:07,362 --> 00:07:09,147
You're admitting
I didn't leak the trailer?

150
00:07:09,181 --> 00:07:11,612
- I am.
- That's why he came here this morning.

151
00:07:11,715 --> 00:07:14,582
- He said you wouldn't call him back.
- He sent an E-mail at 4:00 a.m.

152
00:07:14,658 --> 00:07:17,454
- threatening to kill me.
- Then at 5:00 a.M., my editor

153
00:07:17,626 --> 00:07:20,108
called and told me that he got pissed
at his girl last week

154
00:07:20,186 --> 00:07:23,470
and put a video of him giving
her a facial on cumfiesta.com.

155
00:07:23,704 --> 00:07:25,902
She got back at him
with my trailer, our trailer.

156
00:07:27,008 --> 00:07:29,614
- You're a real asshole, you know that?
- I'm man enough to admit

157
00:07:29,682 --> 00:07:32,105
- when I've been acting like one.
- Admit the other thing.

158
00:07:33,043 --> 00:07:34,439
I love <i>Lost in the clouds</i>, Vin.

159
00:07:34,491 --> 00:07:37,465
I read that book four times. I could
shoot the shit out of that thing.

160
00:07:37,986 --> 00:07:40,572
- We don't doubt that.
- Okay now, so...

161
00:07:41,093 --> 00:07:42,270
Are we gonna make this movie?

162
00:07:42,348 --> 00:07:44,763
Are we gonna go talk to Dana Gordon?
What do you say, boys?

163
00:07:47,566 --> 00:07:49,267
Come on, E!
As much as we fight,

164
00:07:49,335 --> 00:07:51,219
you know I think
of you and Vinny as family.

165
00:07:52,138 --> 00:07:54,391
Want to climb this mountain together?
We'll kill it.

166
00:07:56,272 --> 00:07:57,306
Sure.

167
00:07:57,482 --> 00:07:59,034
Come here, you motherfucker.

168
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:01,713
Would you look at that?
Love is in the air!

169
00:08:01,781 --> 00:08:03,693
Is this beautiful or what, Lloyd?

170
00:08:03,904 --> 00:08:05,637
Come and join us in a group hug!

171
00:08:06,007 --> 00:08:07,688
Could be a while before you get some.

172
00:08:09,365 --> 00:08:11,439
Aw, come on!
I was just teasing, Lloyd!

173
00:08:11,517 --> 00:08:13,625
It was a joke!
I'll be right back.

174
00:08:18,879 --> 00:08:20,302
They don't fuck each other, do they?

175
00:08:20,428 --> 00:08:22,626
Come on, I was just trying
to cheer you up!

176
00:08:22,781 --> 00:08:25,418
There is no cheering me up.
My life is over.

177
00:08:25,573 --> 00:08:27,746
- It's not over!
- Yes, it is.

178
00:08:27,901 --> 00:08:29,704
Without Tom, my life is empty.

179
00:08:30,225 --> 00:08:31,441
An empty vase!

180
00:08:32,548 --> 00:08:35,080
- Why a vase?
- Because Tom was a flower.

181
00:08:35,587 --> 00:08:37,761
He was, Ari!
He was a rose,

182
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:41,609
a bright red rose
in the massive oil spill of life.

183
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:43,497
And without him, everything is just...

184
00:08:43,928 --> 00:08:45,015
Gooky!

185
00:08:45,144 --> 00:08:46,801
- Don't laugh at me!
- I'm not laughing,

186
00:08:46,905 --> 00:08:49,387
- but "gooky" is funny.
- I need to take a leave of absence.

187
00:08:49,543 --> 00:08:51,190
- No, you don't.
- I do! I am...

188
00:08:52,019 --> 00:08:53,855
You're a rising star in this company.

189
00:08:53,996 --> 00:08:56,143
- No time for maternity leave.
- Sorry, Ari.

190
00:08:56,246 --> 00:08:58,212
Lloyd, you're gonna
set yourself back years!

191
00:08:58,737 --> 00:09:00,105
What will I do?!

192
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:04,892
50 grand, huh?

193
00:09:05,371 --> 00:09:08,204
And I'm letting you in on this
because you're my blood and I love you.

194
00:09:08,308 --> 00:09:09,989
and I can only raise 30 grand on my own

195
00:09:10,152 --> 00:09:12,710
'cause the IRS, those cocksuckers,
froze my assets again.

196
00:09:12,787 --> 00:09:15,296
- And so you need 20 grand, then?
- What are you, rain man?

197
00:09:15,425 --> 00:09:16,796
That's what I just told you.

198
00:09:17,292 --> 00:09:18,456
So'd you bring it, or what?

199
00:09:18,533 --> 00:09:20,499
I got it.
It's a check. It's good.

200
00:09:20,654 --> 00:09:21,766
There you go!

201
00:09:22,728 --> 00:09:23,907
Last of my Saigon money.

202
00:09:23,944 --> 00:09:25,729
Just what is this investment already?

203
00:09:25,806 --> 00:09:29,183
- Baseball memorabilia.
- Baseball memorabilia?

204
00:09:29,402 --> 00:09:31,045
Not just any baseball memorabilia.

205
00:09:31,203 --> 00:09:35,740
I'm talking about a Sandy Koufax
game-used home jersey from '66.

206
00:09:35,929 --> 00:09:37,532
50 grand for a jersey?!

207
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:40,299
That ain't shit, Drama. It's gonna
be worth twice as much as that.

208
00:09:40,384 --> 00:09:41,884
- At least.
- How do you know?

209
00:09:41,994 --> 00:09:44,649
My father, the prick,
is obsessed with Sandy.

210
00:09:45,303 --> 00:09:46,510
He bought a condo in st. Paul

211
00:09:46,561 --> 00:09:48,630
'cause Sandy was living
in the same development.

212
00:09:48,785 --> 00:09:50,517
- So?
- So, my father,

213
00:09:50,573 --> 00:09:52,048
the demented fuck that he is,

214
00:09:52,359 --> 00:09:55,281
makes his tee time
the same as Sandy's every wednesday.

215
00:09:55,410 --> 00:09:58,291
- So what, Ronnie?
- So Sandy hasn't teed off in weeks.

216
00:09:58,497 --> 00:10:00,332
Wait, I don't follow, why not?

217
00:10:01,243 --> 00:10:03,571
Jesus christ, you guys
are fuckin' slow, huh?

218
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:05,551
Sandy's finished. He's done.

219
00:10:05,774 --> 00:10:07,138
His place is a hospice.

220
00:10:07,338 --> 00:10:09,898
White coats coming and going
for the last two weeks.

221
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:12,536
Just a matter of time.

222
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,217
Sandy Koufax is gonna die?

223
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,523
Jesus christ, that's terrible.

224
00:10:16,682 --> 00:10:19,549
Yeah, indeed, it is.
My father, he's been a wreck for weeks.

225
00:10:20,275 --> 00:10:21,982
But hey, we gotta make a buck, right?

226
00:10:23,381 --> 00:10:25,502
Could you imagine
being able to buy a Picasso

227
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:28,917
a week before his demise?
We can!

228
00:10:31,297 --> 00:10:33,715
So you can pack the camera in the snow,

229
00:10:33,897 --> 00:10:37,287
have it pointing straight down
the face of the cliff and then...

230
00:10:37,519 --> 00:10:39,200
Vinny's beautiful mug pops out,

231
00:10:39,330 --> 00:10:41,809
just those big blue eyes

232
00:10:42,184 --> 00:10:45,880
with the bright, white snow
surrounding them. It'll be magical.

233
00:10:45,996 --> 00:10:47,859
- Sounds like it.
- What do you think, E?

234
00:10:47,988 --> 00:10:49,307
Sounds great.

235
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:53,600
Hi... Guys.
I'm really sorry,

236
00:10:53,753 --> 00:10:55,625
but I called Ari's office
earlier this morning

237
