Get your ass back to the office
within the hour

474
00:21:13,013 --> 00:21:14,513
and I will stick to that story.

475
00:21:14,591 --> 00:21:15,780
Let me tell you something:

476
00:21:15,884 --> 00:21:17,921
I love a liar, but I hate a cheater.

477
00:21:18,231 --> 00:21:19,301
- <i>See ya!</i>
- Wait!

478
00:21:19,851 --> 00:21:21,300
I can't believe you did this for me.

479
00:21:21,326 --> 00:21:22,786
I like you. What can I say?

480
00:21:22,863 --> 00:21:24,854
Say you'll let me take
you and the wife to dinner

481
00:21:24,906 --> 00:21:27,304
- with tom, a couples dinner.
- I don't like you that much.

482
00:21:27,329 --> 00:21:28,855
Get your ass back to the office

483
00:21:28,933 --> 00:21:31,421
and get that fuckin' dartboard
down off your wall!

484
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:38,987
$62,000. This was supposed
to go for no more than 50.

485
00:21:39,220 --> 00:21:42,401
What's the difference? It'll cut
into our profit margin a bit is all.

486
00:21:42,868 --> 00:21:44,368
Ah, the Koufax bidders.

487
00:21:44,670 --> 00:21:46,377
- That's us.
- You guys big fans?

488
00:21:46,480 --> 00:21:48,450
- Oh, die-hards.
- We're New Yorkers.

489
00:21:48,579 --> 00:21:50,778
Sandy would've been really
pleased to meet you guys.

490
00:21:50,881 --> 00:21:52,433
Such a shame he
couldn't get out here.

491
00:21:52,562 --> 00:21:54,139
Yeah, it would've been a great thrill.

492
00:21:54,242 --> 00:21:56,648
Sad, really.
Hasn't left his house in a month.

493
00:21:57,272 --> 00:21:58,824
Oh, no. Is everything okay?

494
00:21:58,949 --> 00:22:01,225
We'd be devastated
if something happened to Sandy.

495
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:03,535
Sandy's as well as can be expected.

496
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:05,371
His dog's been sick for months.

497
00:22:05,625 --> 00:22:08,082
He did everything he could,
but he finally succumbed.

498
00:22:08,255 --> 00:22:09,393
His dog?

499
00:22:09,584 --> 00:22:11,757
His beloved giant schnauzer, pee wee.

500
00:22:12,249 --> 00:22:14,318
Made it to 19.
That's pretty good for a dog.

501
00:22:14,943 --> 00:22:16,498
But you know what?
Next month,

502
00:22:16,990 --> 00:22:19,163
Sandy's gonna be out here
for the celebrity pro-am.

503
00:22:19,291 --> 00:22:21,360
He's favored as usual...
healthy as a clam.

504
00:22:21,736 --> 00:22:23,339
Maybe you guys can catch him then.

505
00:22:24,276 --> 00:22:25,433
Maybe.

506
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:30,147
I'm gonna kill your cousin.

507
00:22:31,837 --> 00:22:33,001
Kill him.

508
00:22:36,456 --> 00:22:38,432
Tom, you know
I saw and loved <i>Dreamgirls</i>

509
00:22:38,509 --> 00:22:41,665
when it was in the theater, but I will
gladly watch it again with you tonight.

510
00:22:42,613 --> 00:22:43,958
I saw it with my mother.

511
00:22:45,791 --> 00:22:48,028
- Just tell us what our options are.
- Well, let's see.

512
00:22:48,105 --> 00:22:49,847
We can all drink poison gatorade

513
00:22:49,924 --> 00:22:52,071
and hope that the next life
is better than this one.

514
00:22:52,174 --> 00:22:53,648
Come on, E. You drink first.

515
00:22:54,379 --> 00:22:57,172
Vince, you really want
to throw away a go movie?

516
00:22:58,492 --> 00:23:00,690
E, it's your job to help him

517
00:23:00,813 --> 00:23:03,394
to get the movies that he wants,
not to fuck them up!

518
00:23:03,471 --> 00:23:05,799
You know he's helped me get
everything I've ever wanted.

519
00:23:05,877 --> 00:23:09,098
Come on, all right. So, you don't
like it when people talk down to you.

520
00:23:09,201 --> 00:23:10,727
People talk down to me every day.

521
00:23:10,805 --> 00:23:12,997
If I let go of all my clients
that talk down to me,

522
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:14,652
he'd be the only one I had left.

523
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:17,973
I mean, Jesus, man,
after all he's done for you,

524
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:21,067
swallow your pride
and take one for the team.

525
00:23:21,657 --> 00:23:24,569
- Tell him that you wanna do this movie.
- He knows I wanna do the movie.

526
00:23:24,637 --> 00:23:25,942
And he knows that I don't.

527
00:23:26,097 --> 00:23:27,629
Look, I shouldn't be producing anyway.

528
00:23:27,732 --> 00:23:29,618
You wanna do this movie?
I'll sit this one out.

529
00:23:29,721 --> 00:23:30,847
Here comes the Irish guilt.

530
00:23:30,924 --> 00:23:32,370
There's no guilt.
The truth is,

531
00:23:32,473 --> 00:23:34,271
I don't like standing
around on sets anyway.

532
00:23:34,380 --> 00:23:35,637
That's not why I came out here.

533
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:38,068
I'll go back to managing
and find the next project.

534
00:23:38,284 --> 00:23:39,723
Boom! Problem solved.

535
00:23:39,952 --> 00:23:41,452
He goes back to being a manager,

536
00:23:41,654 --> 00:23:43,638
I get him paid as a producer anyway.

537
00:23:44,234 --> 00:23:45,967
Lottery strikes again for you, E.

538
00:23:46,182 --> 00:23:47,242
Are you sure about this?

539
00:23:47,320 --> 00:23:49,273
And as your manager,
I'm sure of something else.

540
00:23:49,350 --> 00:23:51,567
- Oh, yeah? What?
- You shouldn't be doing this movie,

541
00:23:51,619 --> 00:23:53,164
- not with Billy.
- Jesus, fuck.

542
00:23:53,270 --> 00:23:55,742
And it's not my pride.
It's because I think Walsh has peaked.

543
00:23:55,794 --> 00:23:57,656
And I think
his best days are behind him.

544
00:23:58,273 --> 00:23:59,671
And I think he fucked up <i>Medellin</i>.

545
00:23:59,722 --> 00:24:01,729
- You know I don't agree with you.
- Nor do I.

546
00:24:01,807 --> 00:24:04,134
- You haven't seen it.
- I'm against you either way.

547
00:24:05,378 --> 00:24:07,757
- It's your choice, Vince.
- It is your choice.

548
00:24:07,912 --> 00:24:11,222
It's your life. He's just a passenger
lucky to have a seat.

549
00:24:13,094 --> 00:24:14,310
I'm gonna do the movie.

550
00:24:14,998 --> 00:24:18,489
There you go!
I'll have a $2 million advance check

551
00:24:18,696 --> 00:24:21,231
cut for you today!
How horrible!

552
00:24:22,305 --> 00:24:25,092
Bring in some bubbly!
We're doing a little celebrating.

553
00:24:26,463 --> 00:24:29,010
- Are you sure about this?
- Yeah. I just wanted to be heard.

554
00:24:29,564 --> 00:24:31,438
- Well, you weew.
- Yeah, I guess I was.

